{
  "about": [
    "Shared vectors for the canopy push grammar and the forbidden-character predicate.",
    "Authored in canopy (tests/canopy_mcp/fixtures/grammar-vectors.json); every other holder keeps a byte-identical copy.",
    "ASCII-only: forbidden characters are spelled as \\u escapes, a lone surrogate included. No trailing whitespace, one final newline.",
    "A segment is accepted when it fullmatches its pattern and is not reserved; every reserved rule compares segment.casefold().",
    "Every case runs with reserved.configuredNames as the deployment's own reserved names (CANOPY_LIBRARY_IGNORED_NAMES); without them those names are free.",
    "A character is forbidden when it is C0 other than tab, LF and CR, DEL, C1, a bidi control, any other format character (category Cf) or a lone surrogate (category Cs).",
    "A pointer is the RFC 6901 pointer of the first string, in document order, that holds a forbidden character; an offending object key reports the pointer of the object that holds it; null means none.",
    "Casefold collisions are taken over the member paths plus every directory prefix of them; each collision lists its spellings sorted by code point, and a single spelling is a path that is both a member and a directory."
  ],
  "patterns": {
    "idSegment": "[A-Za-z0-9_-]+",
    "assetSegment": "[A-Za-z0-9 ._-]+"
  },
